@startuml codeemb-ensemble
' EnsembleCodeEmbedder: members are queried sequentially, their vectors are fused by
' one of four strategies, and the result is L2-normalized. Only Concatenate changes
' the dimension; the other three require every member to agree on d.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/codeemb-ensemble.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/code-embeddings/ensemble.md.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title Ensemble — combine_embeddings(v₁ … v_N) under four strategies

rectangle "**(code c, language ℓ)**" as q #EF6C00

rectangle "**CodeT5Embedder**\nv₁ ∈ ℝ²⁵⁶" as m1 #2E7D32
rectangle "**UniXcoderEmbedder**\nv₂ ∈ ℝ⁷⁶⁸" as m2 #388E3C
rectangle "**GraphCodeBertEmbedder**\nv₃ ∈ ℝ⁷⁶⁸" as m3 #43A047

rectangle "**EnsembleStrategy**\n(one of four)" as strat #6A1B9A

rectangle "**Concatenate**  (default)\nv = [v₁ │ v₂ │ … │ v_N]\nd = Σᵢ dᵢ" as cat #6A1B9A
rectangle "**WeightedAverage**\nv = Σᵢ wᵢ · vᵢ\nweights **not** renormalized" as wavg #6A1B9A
rectangle "**MeanPooling**\nv = (1∕N) · Σᵢ vᵢ" as mean #6A1B9A
rectangle "**MaxPooling**\nvₖ = maxᵢ vᵢₖ  (coordinate-wise)" as max #6A1B9A

rectangle "**L2 normalize**\nnormalize_final (default true)" as norm #2E7D32
rectangle "**v̂ ∈ ℝᵈ**\nd = 1792 concat │ 768 otherwise" as out #455A64

q --> m1
q --> m2
q --> m3
m1 --> strat
m2 --> strat
m3 --> strat
strat --> cat
strat --> wavg
strat --> mean
strat --> max
cat --> norm
wavg --> norm
mean --> norm
max --> norm
norm --> out

note bottom of strat #F3E5F5
  ""with_strategy"" **rejects** unequal dimensions for
  every strategy except Concatenate, so CodeT5+ (256)
  cannot be averaged with the two 768-d models.
end note

note right of cat #E8F5E9
  With unit-norm members, concatenate-then-normalize
  makes the ensemble cosine the **unweighted mean of the
  member cosines** — see (E4) in ensemble.md.
end note

note left of m1 #FFF3E0
  Members run **sequentially** on the calling
  thread (""iter().map(...)""), so ensemble
  latency ≈ Σᵢ latency(modelᵢ).
end note

@enduml
